     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Block configSecret:credentialAccess and ssoLogin:authenticate. Blocking configSecret cuts dbLogin (an AND step), which cuts jumpHost, which cuts vaultRead. Together with ssoLogin, it also removes every parent of monitoringHost. That cuts codeRepo, localAdmin and serviceAccount, so dbReplica is unreachable. Blocking ssoLogin also cuts secretsManager (an AND step), so shareMount is unreachable. All four parents of crownData are then unreachable. One block is not enough. Blocking monitoringHost leaves jumpHost reachable via dbLogin. Blocking configSecret alone leaves monitoringHost reachable via ssoLogin. ssoLogin, configSecret and secretsManager are each reachable directly from footholds, so no single step blocks every path.\"}"
    }
   ],
